  m_text: 'Dear hero,

    I write to you with sorrow in my heart. Dahak has once
    again struck our kingdom, capturing our allies and leaving the survivors in hiding.
    They have called upon your strength to venture into the cold and rescue those
    we have lost.

    Dahak is exceedingly dangerous. He has set treacherous traps
    along the frozen paths, so you must tread with the utmost caution.

    Troy,
    our last brave adventurer, has set out before you to scout the wilderness and
    clear a safe path. However, the blizzards are fierce and the terrain is hostile;
    it takes Troy time to navigate the snow and find a safe passage. Do not rush,
    as he can only secure one new passage each day.

    The spirits of the North
    watch your deeds closely, and your honor will grow for every companion you return
    to safety. Time is of the essence; the faster you navigate the frozen wastes,
    the greater your renown. Yet, guard your strength well. Every time you fall and
    must restart your journey, your standing will diminish slightly, as we value
    swift and decisive triumphs.

    May the light guide your steps...'
